<title>NETHERLANDS: Unilever Q3 net profit Dfl 1.31 billion.</title>
<headline>Unilever Q3 net profit Dfl 1.31 billion.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Third quarter 1996.</p>
<p>(millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (guilders)	   4.68   vs    4.38</p>
<p>    Net profit/current exchange rates     1,313  vs    1,224</p>
<p>    Net profit/constant exchange rates    1,282  vs    1,230</p>
<p>    Interim Div Unilever NV (guilders)    2.23   vs    1.48</p>
<p>    Turnover				     22,120  vs   20,711</p>
<p>    Operating profit			    2,241  vs    2,133</p>
<p>NOTES - Analysts had expected Unilever to report a third quarter net profit of 1.15 to 1.33 billion guilders.  </p>
<p>    Income from fixed investments		15  vs	 41</p>
<p>    Interest charges				165  vs	186</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit				2,091  vs    1,988</p>
<p>    Tax						 734  vs	711</p>
<p>    Post-tax profit			     1,357  vs    1,277</p>
<p>    Minority interests (loss)		    75  vs(loss) 47</p>
<p>NOTES - Unilever said it took a Q3 net exceptional charge of 81 million guilders to cover restructuring at the recently-acquired Diversey industrial cleaning business.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
